  "definition": "The Enhanced Vegetation Index (EVI) is a spectral vegetation index designed to reduce canopy-background and aerosol effects and to retain more sensitivity than NDVI in dense vegetation. It remains a calculation from corrected reflectances. \u201cEnhanced\u201d describes those algorithm goals; it does not make EVI a direct measurement of biomass, leaf area, crop health or drought.[^1][^2]",
